ágrafo."],["Dana","And the closing?","E o fecho?"],["Eli","One plain sentence of commitment.","Uma frase simples de compromisso."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Ajuste refinado de entonação","items":[{"label":"Ajuste refinado de entonação","note":"Ajuste refinado de entonação: pequenas variações de altura e de ritmo mudam a atitude (cortesia, ironia, reserva, compromisso) sem mudar as palavras.","words":["I suppose that’s one way to put it. ↘↗ (reserva)","Well, that’s ONE way to put it. ↘ (ironia)","I’d be delighted. ↗↘ (cortesia calorosa)"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Give a rough proportion.","pt":"Diga.","model":"Roughly a fifth of the text is the opening."},{"q":"State a limit.","pt":"Estabeleça.","model":"Keep it to no more than 300 words."},{"q":"Say who and by when.","pt":"Diga.","model":"The director will report by Friday."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a text infographic (5 items) on how to structure a short apology statement, with proportions.","model":"Opening: lead with the apology (roughly a fifth). Cause: one sentence, plain words. Impact: name those affected. Remedy: say what will change and by when. Closing: end on commitment, not defense.","checklist":["Usei **proporções**","Usei **by when**"],"words":"5 itens"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “statement anatomy” mean?","opts":["ideia central","anatomia de um comunicado","ordem do mais importante primeiro"],"ans":1,"why":"**statement anatomy** = anatomia de um comunicado."},{"q":"What does “core takeaway” mean?","opts":["frase de abertura","partes afetadas","ideia central"],"ans":2,"why":"**core takeaway** = ideia central."},{"q":"What does “lead sentence” mean?","opts":["frase de abertura","ordem do mais importante primeiro","posição do pedido de desculpa